From 4f52b67cdb2b05a3cb138d0f35443960c2e21793 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 11:25:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webui: stop hiding Broadcom wl driver errors from the System
 Log

The System Log page applies a client-side filter list from
www/ajax/logFilter.json (Main_LogStatus_Content.asp), inherited verbatim
from the vendor. One of its entries is "WLC_SCB_", which suppresses every
WLC_SCB_DEAUTHORIZE line - the exact signature of the Broadcom Wi-Fi 7
driver defect currently being reported across the RT-BE range.

A firmware whose whole purpose is to hand the operator control of their
own router should not hide its driver's errors from them. The lines are
present in /tmp/syslog.log and in a downloaded log; only the GUI view
dropped them, so the effect was to make the one surface most users look
at the least truthful one.

Drop "WLC_SCB_" from the list. The remaining entries (UDB add/update
noise, send_redir_page) are genuine cfgsync chatter and stay filtered.

Also remove logFilter.json from the www `update:` target. That target is
a manual maintainer refresh from the vendor CDN, not part of a build, but
running it would silently restore the vendor's list and undo this. The
file is ours to curate now.

Credit: the filter was spotted by Reddit user AdventurousTravel366 and
confirmed against a downloaded log by littlebighuman.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/Makefile            |  6 +++++-
 release/src/router/www/ajax/logFilter.json | 17 ++++++++---------
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Makefile b/release/src/router/www/Makefile
index 4c8c54770d..d4f280e9c6 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Makefile
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Makefile
@@ -29,7 +29,11 @@ endif # HND_ROUTER && RTCONFIG_VISUALIZATION
 update:
 	wget https://nw-dlcdnet.asus.com/plugin/js/tz_db.json -O ajax/tz_db.json
 	wget https://nw-dlcdnet.asus.com/plugin/js/gameList.json -O ajax/gameList.json
-	wget https://nw-dlcdnet.asus.com/plugin/js/logFilter.json -O ajax/logFilter.json
+# ajax/logFilter.json is deliberately NOT refreshed from the vendor CDN.
+# Upstream's copy filters "WLC_SCB_" out of the System Log view, which hides
+# Broadcom wl driver errors (SCB deauthorize / MLO) from the router's own
+# operator. Reaper curates this file by hand - see the entry in the log-filter
+# fix. Re-adding the wget here would silently restore the vendor filter list.
 	wget https://nw-dlcdnet.asus.com/plugin/js/extend_custom_icon.json -O ajax/extend_custom_icon.json
 	wget https://nw-dlcdnet.asus.com/plugin/js/pppIspList_V2.json -O ajax/pppIspList_V2.json
 	wget https://nw-dlcdnet.asus.com/plugin/js/DNS_List.json -O ajax/DNS_List.json
diff --git a/release/src/router/www/ajax/logFilter.json b/release/src/router/www/ajax/logFilter.json
index 2e404f5ca9..64a6e26428 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/ajax/logFilter.json
+++ b/release/src/router/www/ajax/logFilter.json
@@ -1,9 +1,8 @@
-{
-  "filter": [
-    "already exist in UDB, can't add it",
-    "not mesh client, can't update it's ip",
-    "not exist in UDB, can't update it",
-    "WLC_SCB_",
-    "send_redir_page"
-  ]
-}
\ No newline at end of file
+{
+  "filter": [
+    "already exist in UDB, can't add it",
+    "not mesh client, can't update it's ip",
+    "not exist in UDB, can't update it",
+    "send_redir_page"
+  ]
+}
-- 
